# Explicit, not inherited. Vercel falls back to .gitignore only when this
# file is absent, and 59GB of brand library, retreat photography and video
# now sit inside this folder. Not worth relying on a fallback for.
CydnieJocelyn-Site/
Costa Rica copy/
Family Travel copy/
Fonts copy/
cydniejocelyn/

.git/
.DS_Store
# Local Claude tooling. `launch.json` holds absolute paths to a preview
# server on this machine, and until 28 August 2026 build.py walked into this
# folder and copied it into dist/, so it was uploaded on every deploy and
# served at /.claude/launch.json. Excluded here AND in build.py's
# EXCLUDE_DIRS; the drift check at the bottom of build.py keeps the two lists
# honest with each other.
.claude/

# build output and local tooling, not part of the deployed site
tools/
HANDOFF.md
BRIEF.md
README.md

# Working documents. These are wireframes, briefs and copy decks that arrive
# as folders beside the site, and Vercel serves whatever it is given: the
# build brief was live at /The Build page/files/CLAUDE-CODE-BRIEF.md and
# returning 200 to anyone who guessed the path. Add the folder here the same
# day a new one lands, and never park a working document inside a route
# directory like the-build/.
The Build page/
Greece Retreat/
# Renamed from `Retreats/`. A draft folder whose name differs from a route
# directory only by case is a trap: this project is uploaded from a
# case-insensitive filesystem, so `Retreats/` here could have taken the
# real `/retreats/` page out of the deploy with it.
Retreat drafts/
# Both arrived mid-session on 26 August 2026 and were built on 26 August into
# /a-sounding/ and /the-letters/. The wireframes stay excluded: they carry an
# annotation layer, a notes toggle and, in the Letters draft, a live HoneyBook
# widget pointed at the retired Collective form.
#
# Checked against the case-insensitive-filesystem trap above: lowercased,
# `a sounding` and `the letters page` are neither of them `a-sounding` or
# `the-letters`, so neither draft can take a route directory out of the
# deploy with it. Keep it that way when renaming either.
A Sounding/
The Letters Page/
# Arrived 26 August 2026, 19:07. Built on 28 August into /thequestions/.
# The wireframe stays excluded: it carries an annotation layer and three
# copy variants that are not the ones that shipped.
#
# Checked against the case-insensitive-filesystem trap above: lowercased,
# `the questions` is not `thequestions`, so the draft cannot take the route
# directory out of the deploy with it. Keep it that way when renaming.
the questions/
# Arrived 26 August 2026, later the same evening. Built on 28 August into
# /privacy-policy/, which closes the cutover trap in HANDOFF section 7.3.
# The deck stays excluded: it carries four FLAG lines addressed to Cydnie,
# and a document that argues with itself in the margins is not the document
# people should be reading when they look up what they signed.
Privacy terms page/

# Referenced by nothing. Moved here out of assets/img/ on 28 August rather
# than deleted, because most of them are alternates of files that are still
# in use. See assets/_unused/README.md. `tools/build.py` warns if assets/img/
# grows another one.
assets/_unused/
